    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0559" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">738.3915/228</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">W. W. Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 475</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to the Department’s
                    instruction No. 472 of October 5, 1922, on the question of the Haitian-Dominican
                    boundary, there is transmitted herewith a copy of a further despatch received
                    from General Russell,<anchor n="75a" xml:id="d176-f1"/> together with the
                    Department’s reply thereto.<anchor n="75b" xml:id="d176-f2"/></p>
                <p>You are requested to inform the Dominican Government that General Russell has
                    been instructed to state to the Haitian Government that the Government of the
                    United States expects that the <pb facs="0560" n="440" xml:id="pg440"/>
                    provisional line established in 1912 shall be scrupulously respected by both the
                    Haitian and Dominican Governments.</p>
                <p>The Department hopes to receive, in the very near future, your telegraphic report
                    in reply to its instruction above referred to.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
